      "geometryEvidence": "CPU Blender 4.5.11 inspection measures low: 749 vertices / 1494 triangles; med: 2999 vertices / 5994 triangles. These actual triangulated counts differ from the creator page 3000/12000 claims. Both have UVMap and separate baked diffuse/normal/occlusion maps. Same broad body bounds and fourfold topology density support authored low/medium versions, but low has no skin or armature modifier: not a ready interchangeable animated LOD.",
      "rigEvidence": "Armature has 33 bones, including torso chain Bone.004/Bone/Bone.001/Bone.002/Bone.003, bilateral shoulder/arm/forearm/hand and thigh/shin/foot/foot_tip, plus foot IK controls. No finger bones. med, eye med, cloth and cloth.001 have armature modifiers and every vertex has positive bone weights. Body/cloth have up to 14 influences, non-unit weight sums; future four-weight export needs normalization and deformation comparison. Low body/eyes are unskinned. Leg IK constraints exist; forearm IK constraints have no target.",
      "clipEvidence": "Exactly one action, ArmatureAction, frames 1\u201340 at 24 fps (1.625 seconds between endpoints), 330 curves with keys at 1/20/40. Stored NLA strip spans 1\u201350. Meaningfully changing channels affect torso location and upper-body rotations; lower-limb controls are constant. CPU sampling with NLA disabled confirms planted feet and body/arm sway: plausibly an idle/breathing loop, not an authored walk or attack. No named locomotion/combat/death set exists.",
      "anatomyScreen": "Inspected original preview. Complete stocky troll/ogre with integrated face, broad belly, oversized hands and feet, sculpted muscle and skin folds, loincloth and painted detail. No horns, bovine traits or pasted animal head. Strongest match found. Exaggerated muscle masses should still be compared against the retained skeleton style.",
      "nextStep": "Root preview approval first; medium body is the rigged candidate. A later scoped converter would need legacy texture material reconstruction, weight normalization/influence preservation checks, isolated action baking and separately sourced/derived locomotion/combat. Do not export low and med together. CPU source inspection alone does not establish visual or gameplay readiness.",
